  repos/npm is an on-demand cache rather than a bulk index, so it grows when a
  run asks for a name it lacks; eval/npm/seed.sh and a FILL=1 scale.sh run
  deliberately fill a symlink farm under the run directory instead, leaving
  this tree untouched, and the measured sweeps then run against a frozen
  shim.  eval/npm/close.sh is the one thing that writes into it, copying in
  what its fill passes fetched; any other change of hash means something
  wrote into the checkout.

  This is the final run's snapshot, replacing 907b43b8..., which was closed
  over the npm reading alone.  It is that tree, 5228 packuments fetched from
  registry.npmjs.org on 2026-09-24 between 12:46 and 12:53 UTC, plus 568
  packuments close.sh fetched on 2026-09-27 between 22:17 and 22:27 UTC,
  closing it over the shared and placement readings too.  Of the 2026-09-24
  ones, the 3992 names eval/npm/names.txt lists, which are the queries of a
  scale run, were fetched first; the other 1236 closed the snapshot over both
  sides' cones in the npm reading, 50 by seed.sh's --fill, which also chose
  baseline/roots.txt, and 1186 by a FILL=1 scale.sh pass over every query.
  pac reads them as well, through --cache, so without them the sweep
  reproduces only from one machine's scratch directory.  tarballs/ holds the
  three tarballs npm opens because the version bundles its dependencies (npm
  11.20.0 and 12.1.0, request 2.11.4); setup.sh links them beside the farm,
  where the shim serves them.

  The 568 are what close.sh fetched with pac 757e1fd and npm 11.19.0 over
  every query of the final run -- queries.js's 3962 names and 494 targeted
  ranges and the 25 of baseline/roots.txt, 4455 once the repeats go -- in the
  npm, shared and placement readings and both orders.  Its second pass then
  fetched nothing, and asked for nothing this tree lacks except names no
  snapshot of the registry holds: the git repository esprima#harmony, which
  recast 0.5.27 names (qunit@0.x, remove-try-require, replace-method, in
  every reading), and four names registry.npmjs.org answers 404, which pac
  alone asks for: @prettier/next in the shared reading, and ignore-rules,
  @tapjs/.test-built and @75lb/jsdoc-node23-fix in the placement reading,
  which eval/npm/tolerated-misses lists.  When pac changes, rerun close.sh with it (eval/README.md) and record the
  hash it ends with here.

The cargo sweeps need nothing pinned beyond repos/crates.io-index above: both
of them ask cargo only for a lockfile, which it resolves from index rows alone
and writes without downloading a single crate body.  There is no CARGO_HOME
cache in the universe they answer about, and so none to record here.
